Project Brief

1. What the project is about

The project is an adaptive ML model selection system for tabular datasets.
It checks the quality of the data, finds problems like missing values or noise, then chooses the ML model expected to work best and actually trains that model for prediction.

2. Problem we are solving

Different ML models behave differently when the dataset has quality problems.
So instead of always using one fixed model, we want the system to automatically select a suitable model depending on the data condition.

3. Our proposed solution / how it works

Load a CSV dataset.
Do a data-quality audit to check things like missing values, duplicates, outliers, class imbalance and possible label conflicts.
Create an impurity profile showing what problems are present and their severity.
Test/estimate how different models perform under those problems.
Select the model with the highest estimated combined performance.
Then train that selected model on the actual training data, make predictions, and calculate the final results.

