5. Important features / key points

Handles both numerical and categorical data.
Preprocessing includes missing-value handling, categorical encoding and feature scaling where needed.
Tests corruption types such as missing values, label noise, duplicates, outliers and class imbalance.
Uses Macro-F1 as an important comparison metric.
The final system can save the selected trained model and generate predictions on unseen data.

6. What we achieved

In the primary V7 benchmark, the selector correctly chose the best model in 10 out of 11 conditions.
That is 90.91% model-selection accuracy.
So, 10 passed and 1 failed.
This 90.91% is selection accuracy, not the final classification accuracy of the trained model.

7. Important things for the paper

Primary evaluation datasets: Car Evaluation, Mobile Price and Bank Marketing.
Census KDD is used as an additional source/calibration dataset, not as a held-out test dataset.
Maternal Health is excluded from the primary V7 benchmark.
There is also an earlier broader evaluation including Maternal Health that achieved 14/17 = 82.35%, so don't mix that number with the current 10/11 = 90.91% result.
The key idea of the paper should be “data quality → robustness estimation → automatic model selection → train selected model → prediction.”
